<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 29 May, from 1108 to 1999.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1108 CE <span class="tih-ago">918 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Almoravids defeat Castile and León at the Battle of Uclés</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Almoravid army under Tamim ibn Yusuf defeated a Castilian-Leonese force near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ucles">Uclés</a>, south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagus">Tagus</a>. Sancho Alfónsez, the only son and heir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a>, was killed, and the succession crisis that followed weakened Castile-León.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ucles-1108">Battle of Uclés</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1167">1167 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">859 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Imperial forces rout the Roman commune at Monte Porzio</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Tusculum, imperial forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> under Archbishops Christian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> and Rainald of Dassel, joined by Tusculan troops, routed the much larger army of the Roman commune. The victory opened the way for Barbarossa to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> that summer.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-monte-porzio">Battle of Monte Porzio</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-iii">Pope Alexander III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1176">1176 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">850 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Lombard League defeats Frederick Barbarossa at Legnano</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnano">Legnano</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> and Como, the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> defeated the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> Frederick I Barbarossa. The defeat forced the emperor to accept a negotiated settlement with the Italian cities.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnano">Battle of Legnano</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombard-league">Lombard League</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1453">1453 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">573 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantinople falls to the Ottoman Turks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a 53-day siege, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a>'s army broke through the city walls; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-xi-palaiologos">Constantine XI</a> died in the fighting. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> ended, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> became the Ottoman capital.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1660">1660 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">366 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles II enters London as the monarchy is restored</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On his 30th birthday, Charles II rode into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> to cheering crowds after years of exile. The Restoration ended the republican experiment that had followed his father's execution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1736">1736 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">290 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Patrick Henry is born in Virginia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patrick-henry">Patrick Henry</a> became one of the most powerful orators of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>. His 1775 speech ending 'Give me liberty, or give me death!' rallied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> to arm.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wisconsin becomes the 30th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a> joined the Union from the old Northwest Territory. It later became known for dairy farming and as a centre of the Progressive movement.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1953">1953 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">73 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hillary and Tenzing reach the summit of Everest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-hillary">Edmund Hillary</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenzing-norgay">Tenzing Norgay</a>, a Sherpa from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, became the first climbers confirmed to have reached the summit of the world's highest mountain.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1999">1999 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">27 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nigeria returns to civilian rule</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Olusegun Obasanjo was sworn in as president, ending fifteen years of military government. The date was kept as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>'s Democracy Day until 2019, when it moved to 12 June.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 29 May <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-prince-of-viana"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-prince-of-viana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles, Prince of Viana</span><span class="tp">1421–1461</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gottfried-heinrich-graf-zu-pappenheim"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gottfried-heinrich-graf-zu-pappenheim.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gottfried Heinrich Graf zu Pappenheim</span><span class="tp">1594–1632</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anne-marie-louise-dorleans-duchess-of-montpensier"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anne-marie-louise-dorleans-duchess-of-montpensier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anne Marie Louise d'Orléans, Duchess of Montpensier</span><span class="tp">1627–1693</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-england"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-ii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles II of England</span><span class="tp">1630–1685</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/patrick-henry"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/patrick-henry.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Patrick Henry</span><span class="tp">1736–1799</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tenzing-norgay"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tenzing-norgay.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tenzing Norgay</span><span class="tp">1914–1986</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-f-kennedy"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">John F. Kennedy</span><span class="tp">1917–1963</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 29 May <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-majorca"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-ii-of-majorca.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James II of Majorca</span><span class="tp">1243–1311</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-castile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry II of Castile</span><span class="tp">1334–1379</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/constantine-xi-palaiologos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/constantine-xi-palaiologos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Constantine XI Palaiologos</span><span class="tp">d. 1453</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bartolomeu-dias"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bartolomeu-dias.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bartolomeu Dias</span><span class="tp">c. 1450–1500</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/josephine-de-beauharnais"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/josephine-de-beauharnais.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joséphine de Beauharnais</span><span class="tp">1763–1814</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ba-maw"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ba-maw.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ba Maw</span><span class="tp">1893–1977</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arvids-pelse"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Arvīds Pelše</span><span class="tp">1899–1983</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-noriega.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel Noriega</span><span class="tp">1934–2017</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
